WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.660
Jazz Fest is the [most] beautiful thing that ever happened to New Orleans.

2
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.600
It was really way before its time.

3
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:25.120
You know, nowadays, with Internet and online websites and all that doing,

4
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:34.460
Jazz Fest did that to . . . They had a lot of New Orleans artists got used that would not come down south.

5
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:38.940
People are still afraid to come down south . . . to see gospel music.

6
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:46.060
Now, how I do that, the jobs I had working, the experienced jobs, Essence and working Jazz Fest, as bouncers, and Tipitina’s.

7
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:56.090
People come and look at you and talk to you and then they knew a lot of things was happening here because they’d hear all these things,

8
00:00:56.090 --> 00:01:05.120
like “New Orleans is still like a plantation” and “Blacks don’t have no freedom here.”

9
00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:12.980
But my point is that Jazz Fest opened that and had people coming from all over the world, all over.

10
00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:17.640
And this was before Internet and all of this.
